Pattern 1: Basic FIFO Processing & Data Streams
The foundational pattern for handling dynamic streams of incoming data where older items expire or must be processed first.

1. The Concept
As new elements arrive at the back of the queue, you pop old elements from the front if they fall outside a specific window (e.g., time duration, buffer size).

2. Java Blueprint (Moving Average from Data Stream)

Javaclass MovingAverage {
    private Queue<Integer> queue;
    private int maxSize;
    private double currentSum;

    public MovingAverage(int size) {
        this.queue = new ArrayDeque<>(); // ArrayDeque is faster than LinkedList in Java
        this.maxSize = size;
        this.currentSum = 0;
    }
    
    public double next(int val) {
        if (queue.size() == maxSize) {
            currentSum -= queue.poll(); // Remove oldest element (FIFO)
        }
        queue.offer(val); // Add newest element
        currentSum += val;
        return currentSum / queue.size();
    }
}

